   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="PT">Number of additional herbal medicinal products with access to markets as a result of project support</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="PT">In PRODOC, the information for this indicator would come from ANVISA, the records of companies involved in the production of herbal medicines and pharmaceutical inputs. These inputs cover a wide range, including dry and alcoholic extracts, tinctures, energised products and hydroalcoholic extracts. Until 2022, ANVISA reported the presence of 9 active Brazilian pharmaceutical companies involved in the production of inputs for herbal medicines. This provides a basis for understanding the landscape of registered companies in the sector.
 
Some of the 16 APLs supported by the project provide pharmaceutical, food or cosmetic inputs without being registered with ANVISA. Therefore, information from organizations will be check to validate this indicator: contracts signed between buyers and selected organisations and/or data provided by organisations. This information will allow a full and accurate assessment of the progress of the project.
 
The disbursement of the first instalment of the grant for the implementation of their action plans to improve production processes for the 16 selected organisations started in June 2023. Despite the short time, some of the selected organisations have already started the process of commercialising new products derived from medicinal plants as a result of the project&apos;s support</narrative>
    </description>
