   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="PT">Change in capacity of ILCs to negotiate ABS agreements and protect their traditional knowledge, as measured by (i) Revised  UNDP ABS Capacity Development Scorecard applied to beneficiaries of project training; and (ii) number of additional FPIC and/or benefit sharing agreements (ARB) for genetic resources and associated Traditional Knowledge (TK) registered on SISGen.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="PT">The UNDP Capacity Development Scorecard  In its current form, it is not suitable as a measurement tool for project stakeholders. Therefore, a specific tool has been developed to assess the capacity of PIPCTAFs (Indigenous and Local Community Traditional Knowledge Holders&apos; Organizations) to negotiate ABS agreements and protect their traditional knowledge. The survey will be administered to training beneficiaries prior to the training sessions. The tool will be used to strengthen the negotiating capacity of PIPCTAFs for ABS-related research and development (R&amp;D) agreements.

Training on negotiating access and benefit-sharing (ABS) agreements and protecting traditional knowledge has not yet started. Training will be provided to groups of PIPCTAFs from selected organizations that have business relationships with pharmaceutical and cosmetic companies or are involved in R&amp;D activities with promising plants. Training will also be offered to Technological Innovation Centers and interested companies in the first quarter of 2024.</narrative>
    </description>
